        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b4a35a04-572f-5504-97cb-c4752340bd6b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Fragrant Concubine, Qianlong Emperor\n- Places: Kashgar, China, Taiwan, Singapore, Malaysia\n- Organizations: Han Chinese, Uighurs\n- Products: Princess Fragrant\n- Topics: Ethnic demographics, Chinese legend, Interethnic relations\n\nFacts:\n- The story basis of Princess Fragrant is the Chinese legend of the Fragrant Concubine.\n- The Fragrant Concubine is described in the legend as a Uighur girl from Kashgar who became a concubine of the Qianlong Emperor.\n- Princess Fragrant was produced to improve relations between the Han Chinese and the Uighurs.\n- The Han Chinese constitute about 92% of the population of China, about 95% of the population of Taiwan, about 76% of the population of Singapore, and about 23% of the population of Malaysia.\n- The Han Chinese make up about 17% of the global population and are the world's largest ethnic group, with over 1.3 billion people.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
